  "colors": "UB",
  "identity": "The only deck in this run that can answer a spell before it resolves. Divert Disaster and Unravel x2 are the cube's counterspells, and every other build here filed a coverage concession for the stack class citing a zero-row probe in its colours. Behind them sits Singularity Rupture: 'Destroy all creatures, then ANY NUMBER of target players each mill half their library, rounded down.' Any number includes zero, so the mill is a choice - against a creature deck it is a clean wrath, and on the turn a graveyard is wanted it points at you alone and bins roughly half the remaining library at once. Two honest limits are stated rather than implied. It is a SORCERY, so no counter is held up on the turn it is cast; and 'Destroy all creatures' kills this deck's own Xu-Ifit, which is why Rupture is the reset and Xu-Ifit the rebuild, and why the thesis turn is 9 rather than 8. Bygone Colossus is the one creature that loses nothing to Xu-Ifit's 'has no abilities' clause, and Alpharael, Dreaming Acolyte and Uthros Scanship are what make binning it deliberate rather than lucky - both draw first and discard second.",
